{"id":"mahabharata-1-223","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":223,"title":"त्रयोविंशत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 223 · The hymn of the four birds","summary":{"en":"Each of the four fledglings in turn praises Agni as the mouth of the gods, the oblation and the power within all things. Pleased, Agni spares them as he had promised Mandapala and goes on burning the Khandava.","kn":"ನಾಲ್ಕು ಮರಿಗಳೂ ಕ್ರಮವಾಗಿ ಅಗ್ನಿಯನ್ನು ದೇವತೆಗಳ ಮುಖ, ಹವಿಸ್ಸು, ಎಲ್ಲದರೊಳಗಿನ ಶಕ್ತಿ ಎಂದು ಸ್ತುತಿಸುತ್ತವೆ. ಸಂತುಷ್ಟನಾದ ಅಗ್ನಿ ಮಂದಪಾಲನಿಗೆ ಮಾತುಕೊಟ್ಟಂತೆ ಅವುಗಳನ್ನು ಉಳಿಸಿ ಖಾಂಡವವನ್ನು ಸುಡುವುದನ್ನು ಮುಂದುವರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"चारों बच्चे क्रमशः अग्नि की देवताओं के मुख, हवि और सबके भीतर की शक्ति के रूप में स्तुति करते हैं। प्रसन्न अग्नि मन्दपाल को दिए वचन के अनुसार उन्हें बख्शकर खाण्डव को जलाते रहते हैं।","te":"నాలుగు పిల్లలూ వరుసగా అగ్నిని దేవతల ముఖంగా, హవిస్సుగా, అన్నిటిలోని శక్తిగా స్తుతిస్తాయి. సంతోషించిన అగ్ని మందపాలునికి ఇచ్చిన మాట ప్రకారం వాటిని విడిచిపెట్టి ఖాండవ దహనం కొనసాగిస్తాడు.","ta":"நான்கு குஞ்சுகளும் வரிசையாக அக்னியைத் தேவர்களின் வாய், ஹவிஸ், அனைத்திலுமுள்ள ஆற்றல் என்று துதிக்கின்றன. மகிழ்ந்த அக்னி மந்தபாலருக்கு அளித்த வாக்குப்படி அவற்றை விட்டுவிட்டுக் காண்டவத்தை எரிப்பதைத் தொடர்கிறான்.","ml":"നാലു ഇളം പക്ഷികളും ഓരോരുത്തരായി അഗ്നിയെ ദേവന്മാരുടെ വായ്, ഹവിസ്സ്, സകലതിലുമുള്ള ശക്തി എന്ന നിലയിൽ സ്തുതിക്കുന്നു. സന്തുഷ്ടനായ അഗ്നി, മന്ദപാലന് നൽകിയ വാക്ക് പാലിച്ച് അവരെ രക്ഷിക്കുകയും ഖാണ്ഡവം ദഹിപ്പിക്കുന്നത് തുടരുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.223; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"खाण्डवदाहपर्व","titleEn":"Khandavadaha Parva (Burning of the Khandava forest)","verses":[{"text":"जरितारिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Jaritari said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पुरतः कृच्छ्रकालस्य धीमाञ्जागर्ति पूरुषः ।\nस कृच्छ्रकालं संप्राप्य व्यथां नैवैति कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A wise man stays alert before the hard time arrives; when it comes he is never shaken by it."}},{"n":2,"text":"यस्तु कृच्छ्रमसंप्राप्तं विचेता नावबुध्यते ।\nस कृच्छ्रकाले व्यथितो न प्रजानाति किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the fool who does not notice trouble before it comes is bewildered when it strikes and understands nothing."}},{"text":"सारिसृक्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sarisrikva said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"धीरस्त्वमसि मेधावी प्राणकृच्छ्रमिदं च नः ।\nशूरः प्राज्ञो बहूनां हि भवत्येको न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are steady and clever, and this is a threat to our very lives; surely a brave, wise one is the saving of many."}},{"text":"स्तम्बमित्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Stambamitra said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"ज्येष्ठस्त्राता भवति वै ज्येष्ठो मुञ्चति कृच्छ्रतः ।\nज्येष्ठश्चेन्न प्रजानाति कनीयान्किं करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The eldest is the protector, the eldest frees his brothers from distress; if the eldest does not know what to do, what can the younger one do?"}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"हिरण्यरेतास्त्वरितो ज्वलन्नायाति नः क्षयम् ।\nसप्तजिह्वोऽनलः क्षामो लेलिहानोपसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fire, blazing and swift, is coming to destroy us; the seven-tongued flame creeps closer, licking as it comes."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"एवमुक्तो भ्रातृभिस्तु जरितारिर्विभावसुम् ।\nतुष्टाव प्राञ्जलिर्भूत्वा यथा तच्छृणु पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by his brothers, Jaritari joined his palms and praised the fire; hear how, O king."}},{"text":"जरितारिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Jaritari said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"आत्मासि वायोः पवनः शरीरमुत वीरुधाम् ।\nयोनिरापश्च ते शुक्र योनिस्त्वमसि चाम्भसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the self of the wind, the body of the plants, and the source of the waters; O bright one, you are the source of the sea as well."}},{"n":8,"text":"ऊर्ध्वं चाधश्च गच्छन्ति विसर्पन्ति च पार्श्वतः ।\nअर्चिषस्ते महावीर्य रश्मयः सवितुर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"O mighty one, your flames rise up, sink down and spread sideways, like the rays of the sun."}},{"text":"सारिसृक्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sarisrikva said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"माता प्रपन्ना पितरं न विद्मः\nपक्षाश्च नो न प्रजाताब्जकेतो ।\nन नस्त्राता विद्यतेऽग्ने त्वदन्य-\nस्तस्माद्धि नः परिरक्षैकवीर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our mother has gone away and we do not know our father; our wings have not yet grown, O banner of the sun. We have no protector but you, Agni; so guard us, O peerless hero."}},{"n":10,"text":"यदग्ने ते शिवं रूपं ये च ते सप्त हेतयः ।\nतेन नः परिरक्षाद्य ईडितः शरणैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that gentle form of yours, and by your seven flames, protect us now, for we praise you and seek refuge."}},{"n":11,"text":"त्वमेवैकस्तपसे जातवेदो\nनान्यस्तप्ता विद्यते गोषु देव ।\nऋषीनस्मान्बालकान्पालयस्व\nपरेणास्मान्प्रैहि वै हव्यवाह ॥","meaning":{"en":"You alone, Jatavedas, are fit for austerity; no other burns with it among the cattle, O god. Protect us, young sages that we are, and carry us beyond this danger, O bearer of offerings."}},{"text":"स्तम्बमित्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Stambamitra said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"सर्वमग्ने त्वमेवैकस्त्वयि सर्वमिदं जगत् ।\nत्वं धारयसि भूतानि भुवनं त्वं बिभर्षि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agni, you alone are everything, and this whole world rests in you; you sustain all beings and you support the universe."}},{"n":13,"text":"त्वमग्निर्हव्यवाहस्त्वं त्वमेव परमं हविः ।\nमनीषिणस्त्वां यजन्ते बहुधा चैकधैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are fire, the carrier of oblations, and you are the supreme oblation; the wise worship you in many ways and as one."}},{"n":14,"text":"सृष्ट्वा लोकांस्त्रीनिमान्हव्यवाह\nप्राप्ते काले पचसि पुनः समिद्धः ।\nसर्वस्यास्य भुवनस्य प्रसूति-\nस्त्वमेवाग्ने भवसि पुनः प्रतिष्ठा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made these three worlds, O carrier of oblations, you kindle yourself and cook them again when the time comes; you are the source of the whole universe, and again its foundation."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्वमन्नं प्राणिनां भुक्तमन्तर्भूतो जगत्पते ।\nनित्यं प्रवृद्धः पचसि त्वयि सर्वं प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the food eaten by creatures, dwelling within them, lord of the world; ever growing, you digest it, and everything rests on you."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"सूर्यो भूत्वा रश्मिभिर्जातवेदो\nभूमेरम्भो भूमिजातान्रसांश्च ।\nविश्वानादाय पुनरुत्सर्गकाले\nसृष्ट्वा वृष्ट्या भावयसीह शुक्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Becoming the sun, Jatavedas, you take up with your rays the water of the earth and the juices born of it; then at the time of release you send it down as rain and nourish the world, O bright one."}},{"n":17,"text":"त्वत्त एताः पुनः शुक्र वीरुधो हरितच्छदाः ।\nजायन्ते पुष्करिण्यश्च समुद्रश्च महोदधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From you, bright one, come these green-leaved plants, the lotus ponds and the great ocean."}},{"n":18,"text":"इदं वै सद्म तिग्मांशो वरुणस्य परायणम् ।\nशिवस्त्राता भवास्माकं मास्मानद्य विनाशय ॥","meaning":{"en":"This nest, O fierce-rayed one, is the refuge of Varuna's realm; be our kind protector and do not destroy us today."}},{"n":19,"text":"पिङ्गाक्ष लोहितग्रीव कृष्णवर्त्मन्हुताशन ।\nपरेण प्रैहि मुञ्चास्मान्सागरस्य गृहानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"O tawny-eyed, red-necked, dark-pathed eater of offerings, pass beyond us and spare us, as you would spare the houses of the sea."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"एवमुक्तो जातवेदा द्रोणेनाक्लिष्टकर्मणा ।\nद्रोणमाह प्रतीतात्मा मन्दपालप्रतिज्ञया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the blameless Drona, Agni, pleased at heart and mindful of Mandapala's request, replied to Drona."}},{"n":21,"text":"ऋषिर्द्रोणस्त्वमसि वै ब्रह्मैतद्व्याहृतं त्वया ।\nईप्सितं ते करिष्यामि न च ते विद्यते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are a sage, Drona, and what you have said is the holy word; I will do what you wish, and you have nothing to fear."}},{"n":22,"text":"मन्दपालेन यूयं हि मम पूर्वं निवेदिताः ।\nवर्जयेः पुत्रकान्मह्यं दहन्दावमिति स्म ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mandapala told me earlier of you, saying, \"As you burn the forest, spare my sons.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"यच्च तद्वचनं तस्य त्वया यच्चेह भाषितम् ।\nउभयं मे गरीयस्तद्ब्रूहि किं करवाणि ते ।\nभृशं प्रीतोऽस्मि भद्रं ते ब्रह्मन्स्तोत्रेण ते विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both his word and what you have said here weigh heavily with me; tell me what I may do for you. I am greatly pleased with your praise, O Brahmin, O lord; blessings on you."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"इमे मार्जारकाः शुक्र नित्यमुद्वेजयन्ति नः ।\nएतान्कुरुष्व दंष्ट्रासु हव्यवाह सबान्धवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These cats, O bright one, always trouble us; make them, with all their kin, food for your jaws, O carrier of offerings."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"तथा तत्कृतवान्वह्निरभ्यनुज्ञाय शार्ङ्गकान् ।\nददाह खाण्डवं चैव समिद्धो जनमेजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agni did so, after giving leave to the Sharngaka birds, and, kindled high, he burned the Khandava forest, O Janamejaya."}}]}]}